 "notes": "Collected 2026-11-18 via web search snippets only: tennis-warehouse.com and other retailer sites were not reachable by direct fetch from this session, so every figure comes from search-indexed page text and should be spot-checked on the live page before publishing. USD = Tennis Warehouse (US) regular price, not sale/clearance. Where TW shows a reduced price next to an asterisked higher figure, the higher figure was treated as list price only when it matched the line's normal TW price. Head 2025 lines (Gravity, Radical): TW pages show '*' reference prices of $289 (MP), $299 (Pro/Tour), $269 (Team) above TW regular prices of $259/$269/$239; the TW regular prices were used for consistency with the 2026 Head lines (Speed/Boom/Extreme MP $259, Pro $269, Team $239). If the app wants MSRP, add ~$30. Previous-generation frames still in the catalog (Blade v9, Pro Staff v14, Shift v1, Ultra Pro v4, Prestige 2023, TF40 2024, Dunlop CX 2024) are now mostly on clearance at TW; their original TW list price is given. Changed existing values: 29 Volkl Vostra V1 MP: 202->270; 35 Wilson Clash 108 v3: 224->299; 66 Babolat Pure Drive Super Lite: 199->269; 75 Babolat Evo Aero Lite: 169->199; 85 Head Boom MP UL 2026: 279->249; 104 Wilson RF 01: 259->329; 105 Wilson RF 01 Future: 239->309; 117 Wilson Blade 104 v10: 289->299; 120 Wilson Ultra 100UL v5: 249->279; 122 Wilson Ultra Pro 97 16x19 v4: 279->259; 123 Wilson Ultra Pro 97 18x20 v4: 279->259; 152 Prince O3 Phantom 100X 310 g: 249->219; 158 Prince Ripstick 100 280 g: 229->199; 162 Tecnifibre TF40 290 16x19: 279->249. Kept existing values where no clearly better current figure was found: Clash 100UL v3 259 (likely 279 by analogy with Ultra 100UL v5 $279), Prestige MP L/Pro/Tour 2023 (TW snapshots show 259/269 but also 279/299), Pro Staff Six.One v14 269 (a -13% markdown to $249 implies ~$289 list), Pure Strike Team 259 (current Carbon Grey Team is $269), ProKennex Ki Q+ Tour 249 (TW lists Ki Q+ Tour at $239). Benchmark: GBP = UK retailer 'regular price'/RRP (UK shops nearly always show a discount against it; real street prices run 15-30% lower). AUD = Tennis Warehouse Australia list price. CAD = Merchant of Tennis or Racquet Guys regular price. Doubts: Merchant of Tennis Yonex pages (EZONE 100 C$359, VCORE 98 C$359, Percept 97 C$349) were flagged as old cached pages; ATR Sports also showed $305 for Yonex but its en-us storefront may be USD, so it was not used. VCORE 98 AUD listing (Ruby Red) not explicitly labelled 2026 but Ruby Red is the 2026 cosmetic. Burn 100S v6: no Canadian listing found (cad null); GBP figure is for the strung version. Tennis Warehouse Europe did not expose GBP pricing in results, so UK figures come from All Things Tennis, Tennisnuts and Tennis-Point UK."
